This looks like January 2021. Unemployment is 6.7% (December 2020), the fed funds rate is 0.07%, the 10-year yield is 1.07% and the 2-year is 0.12%. The VIX is at 30, which fits late January 2021 (the GameStop episode). US large-cap equity returned -0.4% over the month, also consistent with January 2021. Long Treasuries fell 3.3% over the month, consistent with rising yields. The 3-month average payroll change of +283k is also consistent with the volatile post-COVID readings.

CPI at 1.29% year over year matches December 2020 (1.4%) or thereabouts. Industrial production at -3.58% year over year matches December 2020. Gold is down 2.1% over the month, which also matches January 2021.

